# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## What this is

A teaching/reference fullstack Go app (`[[.ModulePath]]`, Go 1.26).
Domain is per-user **notes**; the point is the *patterns*, not the domain. Full design
in `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-05-go-fullstack-reference-design.md`; phase-by-phase
progress in `docs/TASKS.md`.

Stack: Echo v4 · templ · htmx + Alpine · sqlx + pgx · Postgres 17 · goose (embedded) ·
go-playground/validator · golang-jwt v5 · swaggo/Swagger UI · slog.

## Commands

```sh
make db-up              # start Postgres 17 in docker (host port 5432)
make run                # generate code + migrate + serve on :8080
make dev                # live-reload dev server (air): rebuild on .go/.templ changes
make test               # unit tests only (no DB)
make test-integration   # repository tests vs real Postgres (build tag: integration)
make test-e2e           # full-app e2e tests (build tag: e2e)
make generate           # templ generate + swag init  (run after editing .templ/annotations)
make migrate-create name=foo   # new goose migration
go test -run TestName ./internal/features/note/   # a single test
```

Integration/e2e tests read `TEST_DATABASE_URL` and **skip** if it's unset; `make` loads
it from `.env`. Postgres runs on **5432**.

## Architecture (the non-obvious parts)

- **Feature-based vertical slices.** Each `internal/features/<name>/` owns its full
  stack (model, repository, service, handlers, views) and self-registers via
  `Module.Mount(*echo.Group)`. Shared infra is in `internal/platform/*`.
- **Two surfaces, one core.** Each feature has `web_handler.go` (htmx/templ) AND
  `api_handler.go` (JSON, swaggo-annotated) that call the **same `service.go`**. Put
  business logic in the service, never in a handler — otherwise the surfaces drift.
- **`internal/app/Build`** wires everything and is reused by both `cmd/web` and the e2e
  tests. Add a new feature module here.
- **Cross-feature dependency is explicit**: `auth` exports `RequireAuth` /
  `RequireAuthWeb`; `note.NewModule` receives them as injected `echo.MiddlewareFunc`.
- **Errors**: services return `internal/platform/apperr` domain errors (Kind-based);
  the central handler in `httpserver/errors.go` maps them to JSON (for `/api/*`) or an
  HTML page (web). Don't return raw HTTP errors from services.
- **templ views are colocated in the feature package** (not a sub-package) so they can
  use the feature's own types without an import cycle. After editing `.templ`, run
  `make generate` (or `make run`).
- **Auth**: access + refresh JWTs in HTTP-only cookies; refresh token hash stored in
  `refresh_tokens` for rotation + reuse detection. Email is carried in the JWT claims
  to avoid a per-request DB lookup.

## Conventions

- Generated files (`*_templ.go`, `docs/swagger/`) **are committed** so `go build ./...`
  works after clone. Regenerate with `make generate` when you change sources.
- New DB access goes through a feature's `Repository` **interface** (enables the mock
  in `*_test.go`); add the sqlx implementation alongside.
- CSRF middleware guards web routes and skips `/api`, `/static`, `/swagger`, `/healthz`.
  The JSON API is exempt by design (non-browser clients).
